  "ingredients": [
    "0.75 cup maple syrup",
    "0.25 cup low sodium soy sauce",
    "1 tablespoon Dijon mustard",
    "12 large sea scallops, halved",
    "12 slices smoked bacon, halved",
    "24 toothpicks",
    "2 tablespoons brown sugar"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Whisk maple syrup, soy sauce, and Dijon mustard together in a glass or ceramic bowl. Add scallops; toss to evenly coat. Cover the bowl with plastic wrap and marinate in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/qpC-mkUig5cm5hT04A2IYyfEuUw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/159945-marinated-scallops-wrapped-in-bacon-pifs-ddmfs-step-02-3d8fd6b9cb1b4eaa8b875ede141abac6.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/159945/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Line a rimmed baking sheet with aluminum foil. Lay bacon strips in a single layer on prepared baking sheet, making sure they do not overlap.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/iBDCimw0Eiy-IfCrRFdcnUJiLa8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/159945-marinated-scallops-wrapped-in-bacon-pifs-ddmfs-step-03-a55b1e2570344b728fef072dd4379edb.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/159945/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until some grease has rendered from bacon, yet still very soft and pliable, about 8 minutes. Drain bacon strips on paper towels. Drain or wipe grease from the baking sheet.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/3pxzU5oj_28bHxcQMqnA1CFPLok=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/159945-marinated-scallops-wrapped-in-bacon-pifs-ddmfs-step-04-73c1d2d0880341dfb8922f51f2b5610c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/159945/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wrap each scallop half with a halved bacon strip; secure with a toothpick. Place onto baking sheet. Sprinkle scallops with brown sugar.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/OqH7kZpPZY_YsldrOEgBFinKVK4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/159945-marinated-scallops-wrapped-in-bacon-pifs-ddmfs-step-05-38489e8c137d46638c14872d4337583f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/159945/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until scallops opaque and bacon crisp, 10 to 15 minutes, turning once halfway through. Scallops should reach an internal temperature of 145 degrees F (63 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/DWuYw5g7HcPhzfjMaGZiXudWLQk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/159945-marinated-scallops-wrapped-in-bacon-pifs-ddmfs-step-06-05d039d691ae490dbfea30a25f9fe742.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/159945/step_06.webp"
    }
  ],
